WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.283
Gerald didn't know what to say to the Ugly-Wugly.

2
00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:25.096
"You want a hotel?" he finally said.

3
00:00:25.097 --> 00:00:29.181
"A good hotel," said the middle-aged gentleman.

4
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:32.528
"I'm sorry, but the hotels here shut early.

5
00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:34.742
They're all closed now."

6
00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:38.995
Gerald had said the first thing that came into his head.

7
00:00:38.996 --> 00:00:42.400
He couldn't send these creatures to a real hotel.

8
00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:45.276
They'd frighten everyone in town!

9
00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:49.486
"What about a lodging house?" asked a lady in a bonnet.

10
00:00:49.487 --> 00:00:53.053
Another lady pushed her way to the front of the group.

11
00:00:53.054 --> 00:00:56.881
"Where are the carriages that we ordered?"

12
00:00:56.882 --> 00:00:59.175
"I don't know, but I'll find out,"

13
00:00:59.176 --> 00:01:02.614
said Gerald, pretending everything was normal.

14
00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:04.254
"We'd better get going now.

15
00:01:04.255 --> 00:01:05.624
The play is over.

16
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:09.273
It's time to close the building and put out the lights."

17
00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:10.598
"Let's get going,"

18
00:01:10.599 --> 00:01:14.648
repeated the gentleman, who seemed to be the leader of the group.

19
00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:22.471
He stepped toward the front door.

20
00:01:22.472 --> 00:01:27.664
"I can go with you and help you find a place to stay," said Gerald.

21
00:01:27.665 --> 00:01:30.760
"But you'll have to wait a few moments in the backyard."

22
00:01:30.761 --> 00:01:33.283
The Ugly-Wuglies grumbled.

23
00:01:33.284 --> 00:01:38.334
For some reason they didn't like that idea.

24
00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:42.226
"It's a very nice backyard," Gerald said.

25
00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:44.680
"The pump was just painted green."

26
00:01:44.681 --> 00:01:49.575
The Ugly-Wuglies seemed interested in the fresh paint.

27
00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:53.383
Gerald led them out into the backyard.

28
00:01:53.384 --> 00:01:56.351
He hoped no one would see them.

29
00:01:56.352 --> 00:02:01.015
"I hate to make you wait," he said, inventing an excuse.

30
00:02:01.016 --> 00:02:03.227
"But my uncle is quite insane.

31
00:02:03.228 --> 00:02:05.278
I have to give him his supper now.

32
00:02:05.279 --> 00:02:10.284
When he sees strangers—even nice ones like you—he gets quite upset.

33
00:02:10.285 --> 00:02:12.883
So please wait right here."

34
00:02:12.884 --> 00:02:16.433
"Perhaps we should try to find a hotel ourselves?"

35
00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.614
the lady in the bonnet said nervously.

36
00:02:19.615 --> 00:02:23.866
"Oh no," Gerald said, acting very serious.

37
00:02:23.867 --> 00:02:26.023
"The police arrest all strangers.

38
00:02:26.024 --> 00:02:28.470
It's a new law."

39
00:02:28.471 --> 00:02:32.825
As Gerald went back into the school, he heard the creatures muttering.

40
00:02:32.826 --> 00:02:36.911
They said things like "quite the polite young gentleman."

41
00:02:36.912 --> 00:02:41.389
Although the creatures looked horrible, Gerald wasn't afraid.

42
00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.588
He knew it was because he was wearing the ring.

43
00:02:44.589 --> 00:02:51.071
As long as he didn't touch them, he could be brave.

44
00:02:51.072 --> 00:02:54.195
He found the other children in the dining room.

45
00:02:54.196 --> 00:02:56.855
He didn't want them to be afraid.

46
00:02:56.856 --> 00:03:01.383
"This is such fun!" he said in a cheerful voice.

47
00:03:01.384 --> 00:03:04.190
"The Ugly-Wuglies are just like real people.

48
00:03:04.191 --> 00:03:07.094
They're quite kind and jolly."

49
00:03:07.095 --> 00:03:10.770
"Fun?" Kathleen said doubtfully.

50
00:03:10.771 --> 00:03:14.592
Gerald told them about the need for a hotel.

51
00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:19.854
"Wait here while I go up to talk to Mademoiselle and Eliza."

52
00:03:19.855 --> 00:03:23.009
He ran upstairs.

53
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.960
"I wonder what lies he's telling them," said Jimmy.

54
00:03:27.961 --> 00:03:34.005
Gerald came down again and said that he'd walk Mabel home.

55
00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:38.825
"What about a hotel for the Ugly-Wuglies?" she reminded him.

56
00:03:38.826 --> 00:03:41.084
"Is there a place on the castle grounds?

57
00:03:41.085 --> 00:03:48.395
I need to put them somewhere until the charm breaks," said Gerald.

58
00:03:48.396 --> 00:03:51.060
"Then they'll just be a pack of coats and things.

59
00:03:51.061 --> 00:03:54.103
And we can carry those home later."

60
00:03:54.104 --> 00:03:59.746
"There's a secret passage in the Temple of Flora," said Mabel.

61
00:03:59.747 --> 00:04:02.887
Right then an Ugly-Wugly opened the back door.

62
00:04:02.888 --> 00:04:05.897
He looked in anxiously.

63
00:04:05.898 --> 00:04:09.008
"We'd better go," said Gerald.

64
00:04:09.009 --> 00:04:11.604
He went outside with Mabel.

65
00:04:11.605 --> 00:04:13.215
"This is my friend Mabel.

66
00:04:13.216 --> 00:04:16.940
She played the princess in the play."

67
00:04:16.941 --> 00:04:20.205
The middle-aged Ugly-Wugly shook her hand.

68
00:04:20.206 --> 00:04:23.187
The one in the bonnet took Mabel's arm.

69
00:04:23.188 --> 00:04:27.857
"You clever thing. Do walk with me."

70
00:04:27.858 --> 00:04:31.946
And so they walked through town like any other group of people.

71
00:04:31.947 --> 00:04:39.717
Mabel had to keep telling herself that the creatures weren't real.

72
00:04:39.718 --> 00:04:43.174
They passed only one man who stared at them.

73
00:04:43.175 --> 00:04:47.555
But he just muttered to himself.

74
00:04:47.556 --> 00:04:51.527
At last they reached the gates to the castle grounds.

75
00:04:51.528 --> 00:04:54.729
Gerald tried to open the gates, but couldn't.

76
00:04:54.730 --> 00:05:00.581
They were locked.
